    ('H-010', 'Billing', 'Per-company billing mode', 'tenants.billing_mode defaults to direct_meta; partner_billed cannot be set by tenant code (column grants).', 'Partner agreement for partner_billed.', '1/5', 'Isolation test: tenant cannot change billing mode.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-011', 'Inbox', 'SLA timers, business hours, CSAT, collision warnings', 'Reply-due timers in the inbox from the company first-response target, paused outside business hours (weekly schedule and closed days in the company time zone, daylight-saving aware) and a longest-waiting order; CSAT surveys after a member resolves (three reply buttons, sent only inside the service window to contacts who have not opted out, at most once a day per conversation, re-checked at send time; the first tap is the answer and never reopens the conversation); collision warning: a reply is refused once when another member replied after the sender’s last seen message. Presence indicators and per-team SLA targets are not built; provider traffic is verified against the Graph stand-in only.', 'Connected number.', '3', 'Unit tests (business-time arithmetic, 23- and 25-hour days, timers); integration tests (timers, CSAT payload checked against Meta’s spec limits by the stand-in, taps, skips, send-time opt-out, collision); e2e.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-012', 'CRM', 'Deals, pipelines, tasks, reminders, activity history', 'Pipelines (company settings, audited) with ordered stages and one currency each, archived instead of deleted; deals linked to a contact for life and optionally to the conversation they came from, with exact values in the currency’s minor unit, an owner, stage moves, won and lost (with a reason) and reopening, all with optimistic concurrency; a board per pipeline with owner filters and totals per stage; tasks assigned to members with CRM access, about a contact or a deal, with due times and a reminder emailed once to the assignee (durable job plus a minute sweep; skipped with a reason when the task closed, the assignee lost access or it is over a day late); notes; an append-only timeline per contact and deal; CRM panels on the contact page and next to a conversation; deal outcomes, win rate, time to win and the open pipeline in reports and CSV. Erasure deletes the contact’s timeline, notes and tasks and blanks deal text, keeping outcomes for reports. Custom deal fields, deal import, forecasting and CRM connectors are not built.', 'Production SMTP provider for reminder emails.', '4', 'Unit tests (amount parsing and formatting, day boundaries across daylight saving); integration tests (pipelines, stage moves, won/lost/reopen, versions, conversation visibility, timeline, reminders exactly once with a fixed clock, the sweep for active companies only, erasure, deals report, isolation); e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium (pipeline, deal from a contact and from a conversation, stage move, task with a reminder email through Mailpit, note, won, board, tasks, reports).', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-013', 'Contacts', 'Consent provenance, suppression list, formula-safe export', 'Append-only consent events with source, actor and evidence; company suppression list (adding needs contacts.write, removing needs settings permission); CSV export neutralises formula triggers (=, +, -, @, tab, CR) except validated E.164 numbers.', '—', '3', 'Opt-out and suppression recorded after queueing stop the send (integration); export test with =HYPERLINK payloads (integration and e2e).', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-019', 'Contacts', 'Safe contact merge', 'Merging two contacts keeps identities, conversations and consent history.', '—', '3', 'Merge keeps every identity and the stricter consent.', 'planned'),
    ('H-021', 'Campaigns', 'Campaign approval and sending authority', 'Optional four-eyes approval: a member with campaigns.approve other than the submitter; sends run under the submitter’s (or resuming member’s) authority and pause when that member leaves or loses campaigns.send; history and audit of every transition.', '—', '3', 'Integration tests: self-approval refused, rejection drops the snapshot, withdrawal, launcher losing permission pauses the campaign.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-022', 'Campaigns', 'Campaign guardrails', 'Marketing frequency cap per contact (company setting, counting campaign, inbox and store marketing templates; store messages and automation template steps with a marketing template stop at it too, H-030 and H-031), message cap, estimated spending cap, pacing, sending window, deadline; one runner tick per campaign and per company.', '—', '3', 'Integration tests: frequency cap across campaigns, spending cap pause and resume after raising it, message cap, pacing and early-tick refusal.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-023', 'Billing', 'Provider rate cards and cost estimates', 'Platform staff enter Meta’s published rate cards (markets, calling codes, per-category prices, source URL, effective time); immutable once published (triggers), corrected by withdrawal and a new card; estimates in millionths of the currency unit are upper bounds (list price, every message charged).', 'Platform staff copy Meta’s current rate cards; no prices ship with HyFib.', '3/5', 'Unit tests (CSV, longest prefix, exact arithmetic); integration tests for triggers, role privileges and spending caps.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-024', 'Analytics', 'Report definitions, periods and cost estimates', 'ops.metric_definitions stores every reported number’s numerator, denominator, window, time-zone rule, missing-data semantics and freshness (immutable, versioned, equal to the code registry by test); reports run in one repeatable-read snapshot over whole days in the company time zone (23/25-hour daylight-saving days, skipped midnights); Meta charges estimated only for delivered messages Meta marked billable, priced by the rate card in force, with unpriced reasons listed; automation runs by outcome (test runs left out); deal outcomes, win rate, time to win and the open pipeline per currency (P4-04); retention reports shown as not available with the reason. Reply turns pause while an automation handles a conversation (hand-offs start turns), with new definition versions for every turn-based metric.', 'Published rate cards; Meta pricing in status webhooks.', '3/4', 'Unit tests (periods, exact amounts); integration tests (definitions, costs, denominators); e2e.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-025', 'Inbox', 'Mentions in internal notes', 'Notes can mention members who can see the conversation; mentioned members find them under Inbox → Mentions with an unread count that clears when they open the conversation; mentions of conversations a member can no longer see are hidden; mentions are deleted with their note (contact erasure deletes notes).', '—', '3', 'Integration test: who can be mentioned, unread count, hiding after reassignment, erasure.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-026', 'Automation', 'Durable automation runs with a bot/human hand-off lock', 'Runs pinned to an immutable version; each step is one transaction (conversation lock, then run lock) that applies the step’s effects (bot messages through the send pipeline, contact updates, hand-off routing) and stores the new position, so a crash never applies a step twice or loses one; jobs are signals and a minute sweep re-signals lost signals, reply deadlines and wait timers; budgets of 200 steps, 20 visits per step, 50 messages and 7 days per run, and 10 runs per conversation per hour; a step that keeps raising an error fails the run after five attempts and hands the conversation to people; each bot message must be accepted by Meta before the run moves on or completes, and a rejected, cancelled, unknown, late (10 minutes) or later-failed message hands the conversation to people. One active run per conversation: a member’s reply, an assignment, Take over or a resolve ends the run in the same transaction and cancels bot messages not yet handed to the sender; routing waits while a run is active; an opt-out keyword stops the run; erasure clears captured answers.', '—', '4', 'Integration tests: crash inside a step, a step that keeps failing, Meta rejecting, later failing or not accepting a message, restart of the consumer with the signal lost, concurrent arrivals, member reply while a bot message is queued, assignment, take-over, resolve, budgets, timers, isolation; e2e live run.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-027', 'Automation', 'Automation web requests behind an egress guard', 'One egress client for company-chosen addresses (ADR-042): https only, port 443 or 1024+, no URL credentials, DNS resolved once and every answer checked against private, loopback, link-local, CGNAT, multicast, reserved, documentation and metadata ranges (and IPv6 forms), the socket pinned to the checked address, IP literals checked in every notation, no redirects, no shared pool, 64 KiB/256 KiB/10 s limits, framing and proxy headers refused. HTTP steps are written ahead (request encrypted), claimed and sent once by the automation.http worker outside any transaction, marked unknown and never retried when they may have been received without a result, and cancelled when not made before the run’s deadline (ADR-043). Allowed domains and write-only encrypted secrets bound to a domain are company settings (integrations.manage, audited); customer text in headers can never pull in a secret.', 'Loopback test targets only with APP_ENV=local|test.', '4', 'Unit: blocked ranges and notations, pinning, redirects, limits, headers. Integration: made once under retries and crashes, refusals, timeouts, late results, cancellation, sweep, erasure, retention, settings, isolation. E2E: settings and a live run against a local target.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-028', 'Commerce', 'Store connectors (Shopify, WooCommerce)', 'Companies connect Shopify stores through HyFib’s Shopify app (a signed callback bound to the member who started it, read_orders and read_products only, expiring offline tokens refreshed by the worker and stored only if the access was not changed meanwhile) and WooCommerce stores with Read/Write keys (the approval page or pasted keys, proven against the entered address, sent only in the Authorization header over https). Orders of the last 60 days and products (up to 20,000 per store) are read into a copy kept in step by verified, deduplicated webhooks that only signal reads, an hourly read of what changed and six-hourly checks that re-create or re-enable HyFib’s webhooks; amounts exact in minor units; orders shown with the matching contact and next to the customer’s conversation (commerce.read and contacts.read); Shopify’s uninstall and privacy requests (sticky redaction, data requests, shop redaction); removal uninstalls HyFib or deletes its webhooks; contact erasure redacts store orders. Messages on store events are H-029, cart reminders H-030.', 'HyFib’s Shopify app (public distribution for many companies; protected customer data approval for customers’ names, numbers and emails); WooCommerce sites over https.', '4', 'Unit tests (addresses, signatures, amounts, numbers, dates, parsers, HTTP errors); 13 integration tests against the Shopify and WooCommerce stand-ins (handshakes and their forgeries, webhooks, 130 orders updated in one second, lost subscriptions, token refresh and a refresh racing a credential change, throttling, withheld customer data, a signal during a read, uninstall and privacy requests, removal, key handover refusals, erasure, the product limit, isolation; 20 deliberate regressions caught); e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium for both platforms. The GraphQL operations were checked against Shopify’s 2026-07 and 2025-10 Admin schemas. No real store traffic yet.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-029', 'Commerce', 'Order messages', 'Per store and event (order placed, cash on delivery confirmation, shipped, delivered on Shopify, cancelled) a manager picks an approved utility or marketing template, the number, variables from the order with fallbacks, a delay and, for cash on delivery, the confirm and cancel buttons (ADR-048); no rule can be switched on before a manager confirms the customers’ opt-in, and withdrawing it switches every rule off. Events are found by comparing an order before and after each read of the store copy, in the same transaction, and never about orders before the rule was switched on; one row per order and event makes a second message impossible; test orders and events seen over 48 hours late are recorded, not sent. Messages wait for the delay and the sending hours in the company’s time zone, and at send time every check runs again (store connected, opt-in, rule, order not erased or cancelled, number, template still approved and matching the rule, channel active, variables, suppression, opt-outs and marketing opt-in) before one message goes through the send pipeline as a system message. Shopify deliveries are found by reading orders in transit again every three hours for 14 days; a cash on delivery answer counts only from that message’s own buttons in its conversation and never triggers keywords, campaigns or automations. Tracking details are erased with the customer. Cart reminders are H-030; a rule for an order event can start an automation instead of sending its template (H-031).', 'An approved template per message; HyFib’s Shopify app with protected customer data approval (P4-06b); the company’s record of the customers’ opt-in.', '4', 'Unit tests (event detection, send time and sending hours, variables, cash on delivery payloads and buttons, Shopify shipments, WooCommerce milestones); 7 integration tests against the Shopify, WooCommerce and Graph stand-ins (placed, shipped, delivered by re-reading orders in transit and cancelled; cash on delivery taps; the past, test orders, late events, suppression, opt-outs, missing numbers and erasure; sending hours, rules, templates and numbers changed before sending; WooCommerce; permissions, audit, edit conflicts and isolation; 30 deliberate regressions caught); e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium (a rule set up, a new order sent, the customer’s cash on delivery answer on the order). No real store or WhatsApp traffic yet.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-030', 'Commerce', 'Cart reminders (Shopify)', 'While a cart reminder is on, the store job reads a connected Shopify store’s checkouts every 15 minutes with read_orders, only those updated since the reminder was switched on, paged in full, with a cursor that moves to each read’s start less two minutes and never goes back (ADR-049). A checkout left with a number gets up to two reminders (the first 30 minutes to 24 hours after it was left, the second 1 hour to 3 days and later than the first) with approved marketing templates and checkout variables (customer, total, items, recovery address, store name); at most one per checkout and kind, moved while waiting when the customer comes back and never changed once sent. At send time, besides every order message check, the checkout must still be open with no order from the number since it began, at most three days old, the second reminder follows a sent first one, and the company’s marketing frequency cap is counted under the campaign runner’s lock. Customer access (read_customers) is asked for per store only when a manager allows it; the exchanged token replaces the old one (Shopify keeps one per store), and a grant without the connector’s own scopes fails the store. With the store consent setting on (commerce.manage and contacts.write), Shopify’s WhatsApp marketing consent for the customer’s default phone becomes consent events with Shopify’s time, never for suppressed numbers, and the setting is read again as each page is saved. A 30-day report shows reminders sent (not failed), checkouts recovered after a reminder and their value per currency; checkouts are deleted 30 days after their last update and redacted for good by erasure and customers/redact.', 'HyFib’s Shopify app (P4-06b) with protected customer data approval including phone; read_customers allowed for the app when stores use customer access; SHOPIFY_API_VERSION 2026-07 or later for the store consent setting; an approved marketing template.', '4', 'Unit tests (which checkouts call for reminders, delay ranges, checkout values and variables of the other subject refused, consent states, the checkout parser); 4 integration tests against the Shopify and Graph stand-ins (reminders moved while waiting and unchanged once sent, completed checkouts and orders from the number, an older copy from Shopify, the clock margin, the second reminder, three days, the frequency cap, a template recategorised at Meta, customer access asked for, refused, granted without the connector’s scopes and exchanged while credentials changed, the store’s consent imported once and never for suppressed numbers, the setting turned off during a read, the API version and contacts.write, paging past one run, the opt-in withdrawn, read errors kept on the store, erasure and customers/redact by number and customer id, pruning, the recovery report, isolation; 52 deliberate regressions caught); e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium (customer access approved in Shopify, the store consent setting, a reminder sent with the checkout’s values to a customer whose opt-in the store recorded, the recovery counted). The checkout queries were checked against Shopify’s 2026-07 Admin schema (the query without customers also against 2025-10). No real store or WhatsApp traffic yet.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-031', 'Commerce', 'Store events in automations', 'A store’s rule for an order event (placed, shipped, delivered on Shopify, cancelled) can start a published automation instead of sending a template (ADR-050); the automation’s trigger (“An order event in a store”) never matches a customer message, and cash on delivery and cart reminders keep their templates. The rule’s own checks run first (opt-in confirmation, the past, test orders, lateness, delay and sending hours), then the automation (active, its live version starts from order events and allows the rule’s number), the number (active, not suppressed), consent, the conversation (created resolved; not assigned, no other run) and 10 runs per conversation per hour; the run keeps a reference to the order and the event. Template steps send approved utility or marketing templates with variables from the contact, saved answers and the order (number, customer, total, items, status page, tracking, carrier, store), each checked again when it runs (approval, category, variables and quick replies unchanged, the number and its WhatsApp account, erasure, suppression, opt-out, marketing opt-in, and the frequency cap under the campaign runner’s company lock, only tried so a busy lock retries the step); an asking template step branches on its quick replies (payloads bound to the run, step and visit), any other reply and a timeout. Until the customer replies only templates can be sent, which the builder checks on every path. The store’s report and the order page link the run and the run page names the order (commerce.read); a test uses a chosen order (commerce.read and contacts.read); marketing templates need campaigns.send to publish, test or be chosen on a rule.', 'Approved templates; a connected store (H-028) with the customers’ opt-in confirmed for order messages (H-029).', '4', 'Unit tests (the trigger, template steps, payloads of another run, step or visit, the reply rule on every path, order fields, template checks, the warning after a day without the customer); 5 integration tests against the Shopify and Graph stand-ins (an order starting its automation and the customer’s tap, a repeated job, a customer message starting nothing, every reason not to start, every check when a step runs including the company lock and the cap, a conversation resolved later, a deleted order, rule and permission checks, tests with an order, references cleared by deletion and retention, isolation, a keyword automation following up after the window closed, a deleted draft clearing a rule’s reference; 76 deliberate regressions caught); e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium (a rule set to start an automation, a new order, the template’s tap answered with the order’s details). No real store or WhatsApp traffic yet.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-032', 'Billing', 'Plans, entitlements and restricted companies', 'Every company has one plan state (complimentary, trialing, active, past_due, expired, canceled) written only by SQL functions and platform staff, with both audit logs; the minute sweep moves trials, paid periods and grace periods on and emails billing managers; an expired or canceled plan restricts the company (the new restricted status, gated like suspension; suspension wins; reactivation restricts when the plan has lapsed). Limits are enforced by the services and workers where things are added, and modules a plan leaves out lose their write permissions (reading stays) and stop their worker actions (ADR-051).', '—', '5', 'Integration tests (sweep transitions and notices, restriction and reactivation, limits with races, modules, isolation of plan state and counters, function grants), 12 mutation checks, e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-033', 'Developer', 'Public API v1 with company API keys', 'Keys belong to the company and store only the token’s SHA-256 (unreadable by the runtime role); scopes are granted only within the creator’s permissions; a request acts in its key’s company scope as the key (never a company id from the request), writing scopes stop while the company is suspended or restricted, and audit rows name the key. Template sends apply the members’ checks (approval, consent, suppression, erasure, marketing frequency cap) and are re-checked before dispatch; an Idempotency-Key written in the send’s transaction replays the first response. Keyset cursors, 64 KB bodies, rate limits per key, company and failed-authentication address, rotation with an overlap, revocation, an OpenAPI 3.1 document from the validation schemas (ADR-052). A week before a key that can still be used and was not rotated expires, the company’s owners and administrators are emailed once with its name, prefix, author and last use, never a token, and Settings → API keys marks it (ADR-067).', '—', '5', 'Unit tests (tokens, bearer parsing, scopes, error mapping, the OpenAPI document against the route handlers, which keys expire soon and the reminder’s text); 24 integration tests (key lifecycle and guards, authentication, scopes and company status, idempotent replays including concurrent retries, contacts, consent, sends through the Graph stand-in, re-check before dispatch, status, isolation, the sweep; expiry reminders: recipients, once, re-checks in the company’s scope, overlapping sweeps, company status, the kept mark); 16 mutation checks, and 24 more for the reminders; e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium (including the reminder from the worker’s sweep).', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-034', 'Platform', 'Platform operations console', 'Platform staff (MFA) see each company’s health (numbers, quality at the last check, last-24-hour sending and failures, failing webhook endpoints, store, payment account, catalog and Flow failures, dead letters), failed and abandoned signups and stuck number setups, current integration failures labelled by host only, Meta and Razorpay receipts needing attention and quarantine, email delivery counts, pg-boss queue counts with each queue’s retry policy, dead letters recorded by the worker (never the error message; a company only through a verified signature), 7-day review signals on HyFib’s own thresholds and usage over 7, 30 or 90 days. Facts come from SECURITY DEFINER functions that refuse anyone but a platform administrator and read named columns (ADR-054). Two audited repairs: retrying a receipt and resolving a quarantine entry. Alerts, trends, exports and redrive are not built.', '—', '5', 'Unit tests (health issues and levels, signal thresholds, quarantine ids, dead-letter errors and rows); 11 integration tests (each function refusing a non-administrator, the runtime role refused, counts without content, host-only labels, the activity window, signups, receipt retries and their refusals with audit entries, quarantine resolved once, a real pg-boss dead letter recorded once, the 30-day purge) and function grants in the isolation suite; 21 mutation checks; e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-035', 'Billing', 'Monthly statements and payment receipts', 'Billing → Statements lists every month since the wallet was created in the company’s time zone, with credit added, service charges, refunds and chargebacks and closing balances; a month’s statement is computed on request from the append-only ledger in one read-only snapshot (opening balances from the entries before local midnight on the 1st, every line with running available and reserved balances, 100 per page, closing balances that add up), prints cleanly and downloads as an audited, formula-safe CSV in exact rupees. Each paid top-up has a receipt page (receipt number, Razorpay payment and order ids, the method Razorpay reported recorded once by a definer function for the payment that credited it, the saved card for automatic top-ups, refunds and chargebacks) and its billing managers are emailed a link to it (ADR-057). Receipts are payment confirmations, not tax invoices; GST documents, PDFs, stored or emailed statements and staff views are not built.', 'Tax review before live payments (what HyFib must issue for prepaid credit).', '5', 'Unit tests (months, time-zone and daylight-saving boundaries, method labels, the CSV rule for plain negative numbers); 9 integration tests (a receipt with the method and its email, a redelivered payment adding nothing, the method filled in later, a refund on the receipt, receipts only for completed payments, runtime code unable to set a method, months that reconcile across four fixture months, a time-zone change, pages with balances carried over, the CSV rows and audit entry, this month matching the wallet balance, billing.read and company isolation); 29 mutation checks; e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium (receipt, email, statement, CSV download).', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-036', 'Billing', 'Staff refunds of unused service credit', 'A platform owner refunds part or all of a paid top-up from the company’s platform page with a reason (platform audit log); operators see the company’s balances, top-ups and refunds but cannot start one. A definer function checks the owner, the reason, the payment (paid, what is left of it), that the company is not being deleted and, under the wallet’s row lock, the unused credit, then holds that credit (one open refund per top-up). The worker asks Razorpay with an idempotency key and the same body on every try, retries anything uncertain, and checks the refund until Razorpay processes or fails it; the refund is recorded from what Razorpay reports (webhook or check) together with the release of the hold, and a refusal or failure gives the credit back. The company sees the refund in progress on Billing and the receipt, the billing managers are emailed, and statements label the reservation and its release (ADR-058). Refunds asked for by companies, refunds of spent credit, instant refunds and a platform-wide list are not built.', 'Razorpay test-mode run on staging (refunds enabled, refund.failed subscribed).', '5', 'Unit tests (the form’s refund limits, check intervals, labels); 11 integration tests (hold and audit, owners only checked in SQL, amount and unused-credit limits, one open refund, one Razorpay refund across a lost response, 409 and 503, the webhook before the refund id is stored, processed by webhook or check, refusals and failed refunds giving the credit back, emails, statement labels and order, company isolation) and a deletion that waits for a refund in progress; 31 mutation checks; e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium (platform request, worker submission, the company’s in-progress view, the processed webhook). Razorpay traffic simulated by a test-only stand-in.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-037', 'Billing', 'Daily settlement reconciliation (Razorpay)', 'Every day from 06:00 India time the worker reads Razorpay’s settlement report for the previous day (a page of up to 1,000 transactions at a time) and matches every settled payment, refund, transfer and adjustment against HyFib’s records, using the report’s ids only to look up HyFib’s own top-ups, mandates and refunds. A payment or refund HyFib missed is fetched from Razorpay and recorded through the same functions as its webhook (credit only from a captured payment, exactly once); amounts that differ, second payments, adjustments, disputes, other currencies and transactions that are not HyFib’s wait for a platform owner, who resolves each with a note (platform audit log). Paid top-ups that no settlement shows 7 days after the payment are listed once every day in between was reconciled. One run per day, fenced attempts with a lease, retries after 5 minutes to 6 hours for failures that may pass, failure on 4xx; owners can reconcile a day up to a year back or run a day again, keeping what was recorded and resolved. The worker writes only through definer functions and cannot read the tables (ADR-059). Platform owners are emailed once per finished attempt when a day waits for a person or fails, naming days, counts and a failed day’s error only (ADR-066). Alerts for unsettled payments, a CSV export, bank statement (UTR) matching, fee accounting and automatic handling of disputes and adjustments are not built.', 'Razorpay test-mode run on staging with real settlements: the report’s day time zone, item order and paging, and how disputes appear are undocumented (R-110, R-111).', '5', 'Unit tests (report parsing and validation, the schedule, matching and classification); 10 integration tests (runs created from 06:00 and gaps filled, missed payments credited and refunds recorded exactly once, every mismatch class, a day run again keeping resolutions and removing items Razorpay no longer lists, paging, retries and failures, a transient failure while applying, a superseded attempt, platform access and role privileges, the unsettled-payments report); 62 mutation checks; 2 integration tests and unit tests of the alerts (platform owners only, once per attempt, failed and waiting days but not clean or retrying ones, a day run again, a day resolved first, overlapping sweeps, no platform owner, the mark’s own refusals, the email’s text) with 17 mutation checks, all caught; e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium (an owner reconciles a day: a missed payment is credited with its receipt email, the owner’s alert email arrives from the worker’s sweep, and a stranger payment is resolved). Razorpay traffic simulated by a test-only stand-in.', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-038', 'Billing', 'Usage and rates for companies', 'Billing → Usage and rates, for owners, administrators and billing managers (billing.read): Meta’s rates in force for the company’s billing currency (list prices by market and pricing category; a missing price shown as not priced), the next published card with its date and every price it changes, adds or drops (old and new price, difference and percentage), and this month so far in the company’s time zone (delivered, billable, free and not-yet-priced messages, and the estimate by pricing category from the same function as Reports, with the reasons messages could not be priced). Read in one read-only snapshot; drafts and withdrawn cards are never shown; nothing is stored, posted to the ledger or taken from service credit (ADR-060). The email a week before a change is H-042. Per-number and per-campaign figures on this page and a history of past cards are not built.', 'Published rate cards for the company’s currency (platform staff, from Meta’s rate card pages).', '5', 'Unit tests (comparing cards, a zero price against no price, category totals and their order, the change text with minus signs and no percentage from zero, whole prices in currencies without minor units); 3 integration tests (no currency; billing managers allowed, agents, marketers and supervisors refused; the card in force and the next one among drafts, withdrawn cards, volume tiers and another currency’s cards; the switch at the effective instant; this month’s estimate equal to Reports, for this company only, with no ledger or wallet rows); 26 mutation checks; e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium (a company chooses its currency and sees the notice of the change, the rates, what changes and this month’s delivered message).', 'locally verified'),
    ('H-039', 'Billing', 'Monthly API requests and API access by plan', 'Each plan version sets the public API requests a company may make per monthly usage period: empty for no limit, 0 to leave the API out (versions published before keep no limit). Every request that passes authentication and the rate limits is counted in the key’s company scope by one upsert that never counts beyond the limit, and counted without a limit too; a month used up answers 429 with reason quota_exceeded and Retry-After until the next period, a plan without the API answers 403 not_in_plan and refuses creating or rotating keys. The billing managers are emailed once per period; the month’s use shows on the Billing plan card, Settings → API keys and the platform company page, and the limit on the platform plan form and page (ADR-061). Packs of extra requests and per-key quotas are not built.', '—', '5', 'Unit tests (Retry-After, the error reason, the OpenAPI document); 4 integration tests (counting with and without a limit, twelve concurrent requests admitting five of five, refusals uncounted, the next period, plan changes within a period, one notice per period, a plan without the API refusing requests and new or rotated keys, published versions unchangeable and new versions carrying the limit); 26 mutation checks (one through the e2e test); e2e on desktop and mobile Chromium (staff give a company five requests a month, the sixth is refused, the pages show five of five).', 'locally verified'),
